      "source": [
        "### Part 4.4 — Appropriateness: should this system exist?\n",
        "No code in this part — just judgment, which is the scarcest skill in AI for business."
      ],
      "id": "oA2YpXwnUKz7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SPFbTeQIUKz7"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Student Reasoning — Appropriateness**\n",
        "*1. Letters L002 and L006 would likely be declined. If the bank fully automated decisions\n",
        "with your system, who could be unfairly harmed, and how? Consider applicants who write\n",
        "poorly in English but run solid businesses.*\n",
        "*2. Loan letters contain personal data. What are the implications of sending them to a\n",
        "third-party API in another country? What would you check before deploying this at a real\n",
        "Ghanaian microfinance institution?*\n",
        "*3. Name TWO concrete safeguards you would build around this system in production (think:\n",
        "human review points, logging, appeal processes, monitoring).*\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Answer:**\n",
        "1. Business owners with weak English skills, limited literacy, or informal business backgrounds who run profitable, legitimate operations are at risk of getting harmed.\n",
        "\n",
        "How they are harmed: If an applicant cannot explain their business clearly in written English, a fully automated system might flag their application as vague and missing key financial details. They would get automatically rejected not because their business is bad, but because the LLM misinterprets their writing style or missing jargon as a financial risk.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Sending applicant letters containing names, phone numbers, and financial details to an overseas LLM API like OpenAI could violate local data privacy laws. It risks exposing sensitive financial data across borders and storing it on external servers.\n",
        "\n",
        "What to Check Before Deployment:\n",
        "\n",
        "Verify if the API provider uses customer data to train their models and whether data is encrypted in transit and at rest.\n",
        "\n",
        "Check if sending data to third-party cloud servers complies with Bank of Ghana regulations and local data privacy laws.\n",
        "\n",
        "Ensure personal identifiers such as names, phone numbers, addresses are scrubbed before sending text to the LLM.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Human review: The AI should not issue final approvals or rejections. The AI brief should only serve as a draft for a human credit officer, who must review every flagged application—especially those marked with \"missing info\"—before making a decision.\n",
        "\n",
        "Human Appeal Process: Create a simple appeal system where rejected applicants can request a manual review by a human loan officer or submit alternative proof like physical sales receipts, bank statements, or oral interviews if the AI misinterpreted their letter."
      ],
      "id": "SPFbTeQIUKz7"
    },
